# The runs `kjk dialogue sweep k1 MODULE` films a module's conversations
# from: a line each, the module then `kjk play`'s flags that set its story
# up (`--arrive TAG`, `--global NAME=N`, `--talk TAG`, `--made
# CLASS:PORTRAIT`, `--party TEMPLATE`, `--item`, `--skill`) and `--seconds
# N` (how long the run is stepped looking for conversations, 60 by
# default). A module with no line is run once from its entry, its own
# triggers starting what they do, with no party (the Endar Spire's Trask
# is no party member).

# Taris, the apartment: the wake-up asks for a player with a class and a
# gender (k_pend_bedtal), as character creation makes one. Carth stands in
# the module; nobody is in the party yet.
tar_m02af --made soldier:po_pmhc1

# Davik's estate: Canderous brings the party in (taris_escape: Canderous
# forced, Carth).
tar_m08aa --party p_cand --party p_carth

# The Leviathan's hangar: the trigger before Malak's door has his
# conversation object start the scene with the player (k_plev_malacs_en),
# Carth and Bastila with it (leviathan: the party out of the cells).
lev_m40ac --talk lev_invis_malak_conv --party p_carth --party p_bastilla
